<p>“Session” means the cookie is deleted when you close the browser.</p>

<h3>YouTube videos (only if you press “Play”)</h3>
<p>In the Audiovisual section we show videos hosted on YouTube (Google Ireland Limited). Until you press “Play”, the page does not connect to YouTube and nothing is stored. When you press it, the video loads from <code>youtube-nocookie.com</code>, YouTube’s privacy-enhanced mode, which does not use cookies to personalise advertising, although Google may store technical data in your browser to play the video. Pressing “Play” is how you give your consent for that video. More information in <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google’s privacy policy</a>.</p>

<h2>3. How to accept, reject or change your choice</h2>
<p>The first time you visit the website we show a notice so you can accept or reject analytics cookies. Until you accept them, they are not set, and Google Tag Manager is not even loaded. Rejecting them does not stop you using the website or the application.</p>
<p>You can change your choice at any time from the “Cookie settings” link in the footer or from here:</p>
<p><a href="#configurar-cookies" data-abrir-cookies class="btn btn-primary">Cookie settings</a></p>
<p>If you withdraw your consent, we delete any analytics cookies already set. We will ask you again at most every 12 months.</p>
<p>The legal basis for analytics cookies is your consent (art. 6.1.a GDPR). Technical cookies are based on being necessary to provide the service you request.</p>

<h2>4. Third parties, transfers and your rights</h2>
<p>Analytics cookies belong to Google Ireland Limited, which manages them through Google Analytics and Google Tag Manager. Google may process this data in the United States; it is certified under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework, which guarantees protection equivalent to European standards. You can see how Google uses data in its privacy policy: <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.</p>
<p>You can exercise your rights of access, rectification, erasure, objection, restriction and portability, and withdraw your consent, by writing to <a href="mailto:@DatosLegales.Email">@DatosLegales.Email</a>. You can also lodge a complaint with the Spanish Data Protection Agency (<a href="https://www.aepd.es" target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.aepd.es</a>). More information in our <a href="/privacidad">Privacy policy</a>.</p>

<h2>5. How to manage cookies from your browser</h2>
<p>As well as the cookie notice, you can view, block or delete cookies in your browser settings:</p>
<ul>
    <li><a href="https://support.google.com/chrome/answer/95647" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Chrome</a>: Settings &gt; Privacy and security &gt; Third-party cookies.</li>
    <li><a href="https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/clear-cookies-and-site-data-firefox" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Firefox</a>: Settings &gt; Privacy &amp; Security &gt; Cookies and Site Data.</li>
    <li><a href="https://support.apple.com/guide/safari/sfri11471/mac" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Safari</a>: Settings &gt; Privacy &gt; Manage Website Data.</li>
    <li><a href="https://support.microsoft.com/microsoft-edge/delete-cookies-in-microsoft-edge-63947406-40ac-c3b8-57b9-2a946a29ae09" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Edge</a>: Settings &gt; Cookies and site permissions.</li>
</ul>
<p>If you block technical cookies, you may not be able to log in to the application or submit forms.</p>
<p><strong>Changes to this policy.</strong> We may update it if the cookies we use or the regulations change. The version in force is always the one published on this page.</p>
